{
	quest.055BBDD31B8B12BC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Letter and Quills&r work exactly like &bBook and Quills&r, except they have only one page. Good for when you don't want to write a whole novel to send to your friend."
		""
		"When you finish writing, you can then click the \"Fold\" button. This works simiarly to &bBook and Quills&r' Signing, meaning that once you have folded the letter, you won't be able to edit it again!"
	]
	quest.0ECEB6DB82DAA239.quest_desc: ["Scattered around the world, you might come across &6Dovecotes&r. They're simple man-made structures to house pigeons."]
	quest.1033B7FA51F76297.quest_desc: [
		"Before you can start mailing, you will need to find the courier of this mod that will deliver your mail for you: a &6pigeon&r!"
		""
		"They can spawn in mountain areas or near villages. In case of villages, they spawn similarly to cats, meaning you should be able to find them in pre-generated villages."
		""
		"&6Pigeons&r cannot be tamed however! They will follow a player holding &bseeds&r and if there's any nearby unoccupied &epigeonhole&r, they might go in. They also breed with &bseeds&r."
		""
		"Careful, they're hunted by wild cats, ocelots and foxes!"
	]
	quest.13176079F85C751A.quest_desc: [
		"Uh oh, looks like you came across a &6faulty item&r. These items are items that had their recipes stripped and replaced by another similar item. After all, what's the point of having two different tomatoes?"
		""
		"Luckily, you can send these items to &nHorizon Quality Assurance&r and have them replaced with a proper item."
	]
	quest.1ABCEE5D22B9F9B1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Charred Pigeons&r are hostile mobs you can find in the Nether. They sometimes may have a &elost package&r that you can retrieve from them once killed."
		""
		"When a &6Charred Pigeon&r makes its way to the Overworld, it will transform into a regular pigeon, albeit with a charred texture. Likewise, if a regular &epigeon&r gets into the Nether, it will turn into a &6Charred Pigeon&r."
	]
	quest.1ABCEE5D22B9F9B1.title: "Charred Pigeon"
	quest.1B81EED368063E8A.quest_desc: [
		"&dHorizon&r has a mailing system thanks to &6Envelope&r!"
		""
		"With &6Envelope,&r you can find &epigeons&r that then can deliver &eletter&r and &epackages&r to other players on a server."
		""
		"&c&nIt should be noted that the mail network only works in the Overworld!&r&r"
	]
	quest.1B81EED368063E8A.title: "Envelope"
	quest.3227E0A55FEACC2E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Payback Tag&r is a variant of the &eAddress Tag&r, that you can only get by mailing the &nMail Service&r."
		""
		"It allows you to do transactions through the mail network. Instead of sending items to someone else and hoping that they follow through with the transaction, you can have the Mail Service act as the middleman between the transaction. "
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nSeller&r"
		""
		"Inside of the &6Payback Tag&r, you can specify the price of the transaction and how long the buyer has to complete the transaction. You can then slap the &6payback tag&r, alongside an &eaddress tag&r, on a &epackage&r and then send it with a &emailbox&r. Once the &epackage&r arrives at the Mail Service, it will be kept in storage and a &6Payback Box&r will be sent to the buyer."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nBuyer&r"
		""
		"Once the buyer receives the &6Payback Box&r, they can preview what they are receiving from the seller on the left side of the box's GUI. The slots will also show them what the price is so that they can fill the &6box&r with the correct items. After they have filled and packed the &6box&r, they can send it back through a &emailbox&r. Fortunately, the &6box&r already comes pre-applied with the correct &eaddress tag&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nSeller \\& Buyer&r"
		""
		"When the Mail Service receives the &6Payback Box&r, it will send the &epackage&r with the goods to the buyer and another &epackage&r with the payment back to the seller."
	]
	quest.34703414C61627E1.quest_desc: [
		"Once you fold your &eLetter and Quill&r, it becomes a &6Letter&r."
		""
		"Now it is ready to be sent as mail."
		""
		"Alternatively, you can also place it in the world on a wall."
	]
	quest.35C1CCD86A2EB20C.quest_desc: [
		"A &6sealed letter&r or &6box&r need to have their seal removed first before you can open their contents. This can be done by holding right click."
		""
		"But be aware that once you have removed the seal, you will no longer have an indicator of who sent the &eletter&r/&epackage&r. So, make sure you remember who the package is from."
	]
	quest.35C1CCD86A2EB20C.quest_subtitle: "I wonder who it's from."
	quest.379DE51307C04D67.quest_desc: [
		"Before you can send mail, you will need to first specify the address you want to send your mail to. This is done with an &6Address Tag&r."
		""
		"Right click an &6address tag&r to write the address and then hit the &2Confirm&r button. Afterwards, you can right click the &6address tag&r over a &eletter&r or &epackage&r in your inventory to add the address to the letter/box."
		""
		"Writing a player's name is the same as writing the address to their default &emailbox&r. Meaning that if you want to send a player mail and don't know any of their addresses, you can just write down their name and the mail network will automatically redirect it to their default &emailbox&r."
	]
	quest.3D534A15F591B2A4.quest_desc: [
		"Currently, whenever you fold a &eletter&r or pack a &ecardboard box&r, there will be no indication on who the &eletter&r or &ebox&r is from. That's where the &6Seal Stamp&r comes in!"
		""
		"You can stamp a &eletter&r or &ebox&r, by hovering a &6stamp&r over one in you inventory and then pressing right click &8(similar to interacting with a bundle)&r. Once stamped, the &eletter&r or &ebox&r will have your name on it and a stamp with the first character of your username!"
	]
	quest.3EEDF89A1784E0C0.quest_desc: [
		"&dEnvelope&r comes with &6Mail Recipes&r, which are basically virtual address you can send mail to and potentially receive items back."
		""
		"Two known services are"
		"- &nMail Service&r: Anything related to mail items can be received from them. You can receive &ePayback Tags&r, customized &estamps&r and even do a letter broadcast!"
		"- &nAutomated Supply Service&r: They offer some neat recipes for materials that are usually not craftable."
		""
		"Make sure when you're sending items to them, that &cthe items are each in a seperate slot&r. So for example, the &nAutomated Supply Service&r offers a way to convert 6 &brotten flesh&r into 1 &bleather&r. To do so, simply place the one rotten flesh in each slot of a package, pack the box, slap an address tag with their address. You don't have to do this one by one, you can do multiple requests of the same order. So if you want to do 4 &bleather&r, place 4 &brotten flesh&r in each slot, so a total of 24 &brotten flesh&r."
	]
	quest.3EEDF89A1784E0C0.title: "Mail Recipes"
	quest.5E424B3E63691E12.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pigeonholes&r are homes for &epigeons&r. They work similarly to &bbeehives&r, in that pigeons can enter them and will try to stay near their &6hole&r. Good for keeping them where you want since you can't tame &epigeons&r and force them in place. Keep that in mind when you're building your mail boxes."
		""
		"Every now and then, the &epigeons&r will leave <sctrash>\"byproducts\"</sctrash> in their hole... You can clean the hole using a shovel."
	]
	quest.5E424B3E63691E12.title: "Pigeonhole"
	quest.5FF78CC8F0E2478A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mailboxes&r are the way to receive and send mail."
		""
		"Before you can send or receive mail, you first have to setup a &6mailbox&r and enter the mail network. To do that, you will need &23 experience levels&r! When you have the levels, you can then place a &6mailbox&r and name it whatever you want."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nReceiving Mail&r"
		""
		"Any mail you receive will be stored in a list on the left side of the &6mailbox&r's GUI. The list contains information on each mail you received, such as from where it came from, the destination and even a preview of the contents in case of a &epackage.&r"
		""
		"You can extract your mail by simply clicking on them."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nSending Mail&r"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"\",\"extra\":[\"To send mail, simply place a \",{\"text\":\"letter\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},\" or \",{\"text\":\"package\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},\" with an address in the letter slot and \",{\"text\":\"seeds\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},\" in the seed slot. Then wait for a nearby \",{\"text\":\"pigeon\",\"color\":\"yellow\"},\" to pick up the mail and then deliver it. To add an address to your mail, see the \",{ \"text\": \"Address Tag\", \"color\":\"yellow\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"379DE51307C04D67\" } },\".\"]}"
		""
		"This will take some time however, as the &epigeon&r will need to travel to its destination! It's good to have multiple pigeons on hand to be able to handle multiple deliveries at once. The further the distance, the longer it will take. &8(Luckily it caps out at a certain range.)&r"
		""
		"When the &epigeon&r returns, it will be tired and search for a nearby &epigeonhole&r to rest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nDefault Address&r"
		""
		"At the top of the &6mailbox&r GUI, you will find an icon that will allow you to set the &6mailbox&r you currently in as your default &6mailbox.&r This will allow other players to type in your player name instead of a &6mailbox&r's address to get the mail delivered to you."
		""
		"{image:envelope:textures/gui/sprites/mailbox/address_button.png width:20 height:20 align:center}"
		"The icon for when a &6mailbox&r is not the default address."
		""
		"{image:envelope:textures/gui/sprites/mailbox/address_default_button.png width:20 height:20 align:center}"
		"The icon for when a &6mailbox&r is set as your default address."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&nAutomation&r"
		""
		"You are able to automate &6mailboxes&r using &bhoppers&r. &eLetters&r and &epackages&r can be put in from the top, while seeds from the side."
		""
		"You can even extract your mail from the bottom."
		""
		"&6Mailboxes&r will also give out a &ecomparator&r output if they have mail, meaning you can build an indicator for whenever you receive mail."
	]
	quest.6561732C927949EC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Cardboard Boxes&r are a way to store items and send those items per mail."
		""
		"They have 6 slots and once you place an item inside, you can pack the &6box&r into a &epackage&r."
		""
		"These &6boxes&r can also be placed down with sneak right click! Once one is placed, you can right click the box to add more and after enough &6boxes&r, it'll turn into a big one that takes up the full block."
	]
	quest.71C253AB785966A1.quest_desc: [
		"Sometimes, you might come across a broken down &6Mail Hub&r of the Mail Services, floating above the clouds."
		""
		"They're usually way higher in the air, but when they don't survive the test of time, they lose altitude, making them accessible to players."
	]
	quest.71C253AB785966A1.title: "Collapsed Mail Hub"
	quest.7BF0A6C8DB4D4DCD.quest_desc: [
		"Once packaged, you can only remove the items again by ripping open the &6package&r. To do so, sneak right click. Right clicking without sneaking will allow you to peek into what's inside the &6package&r instead."
		""
		"You can also place down the &6package&r by sneak right clicking on a block. Unlike &ecardboard boxes&r however, only one can be placed in a block space. To pick them back up, simple just break them. Sneaking while breaking a &6package&r will instead open up the &6package&r."
		""
		"Ripping open a &6package&r doesn't always return a &ecardboard box&r!"
	]
	task.2163410D21E933B3.title: "Pigeonhole"
	task.263C947328CC04DF.title: "Pigeon"
	task.3CD572483F1A6D59.title: "Collapsed Mail Hub"
	task.47D57BB8EFF4016F.title: "Faulty Item"
	task.4C9C9D3CA7044F47.title: "Kill a Charred Pigeon"
	task.4E653F93056AB0AF.title: "Dovecote"
}
